A||N||3||Seanh||Car ran fine, then wouldn't start. Any Ideas?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||03-31-2001||02:21 PM||||I drove the Fiero into work this morning, and it ran fine all the way in. I go out about an hour later to run to Wal-mart, and it wouldnt start. I poped the trunk and everthing look ok, no loose wires or anything. The car would turn-over fine, but wouldnt fire up. So I grabbed Nates car and went over, bought a spark tester. I came back to try testing the spark and the car started right up the first time. Does this sould like a coil problem? I am sure its definatly ignition related, but Im not sure what components. As in my other topic, I am getting horrible gas milage, so I am trying to get that solved. I am thinking since I am getting bad milage, and the incident that jut happened, it sounds to me like a bad coil to me. I also bought a new O2 sensor the other day and it doesn't seem to help the bad milage problem. I am still getting (according to last nights fill up) 15.88 mpg. I have a lead foot, and every stop light is a race even if there are no other cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I just enjoy driving this car so much after being without it for a while. I am going to order a new MAT sensor from the Fiero Store along with some other things I need. Questions are:<P>What do you think caused the no-starting situation just now?<P>If you think coil (never replaced it since I owned the car, might as well replace it now since its cheap), what brand would you reccomend? Stock/ACdelco, Accel, what?<P>What other factors could contribute to my bad gas milage? (I have replaced: o2 sensor, plugs, MAP sensor, all gaskets from heads up, thermostat(still not running at the right temp though, about 165 and it should be atleast 195), oil, coolant, vacuum lines, EGR tube gaskets. Thats about it. I already plan on ordering and replacing coil, pick-up bobbin, splitfire plug wires(already fairly new), cap(already fairly new), rotor(already fairly new), MAT/ACT sensor, coolant temp sensor. <P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-31-2001||06:13 PM||||I used a Accel coil for 2 years now 30K. Id replace the pickup coil $10 @ autozone and the ignition module in distributor $30 @ autozone. then youve got it all covered.Sensors shouldnt cause it not to start, just run like crap.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||03-31-2001||11:57 PM||||My car acted the same way. Would run fine one day and the next day would turn over but not start. Then would run fine and the next day  not start. It turned out to be the distributor. Mine was rusty and since replacement(about 5,00 miles ago) there has been no problem.<P>About the milage. 15 to 16 mpg with a V6 in town with a lead foot is all you should expect. A four cylinder would be a different story. Otherwise the spark plug condition should tell you if you're running too lean. You know, black from carbon. If air filter clean, timing accurate, spark strong, compression reasonable and exhaust unrestricted your probably getting all the milage you should expect. <P>One other thing. Jack the car up and see if the tires spin freely when you hand turn them. Something could be binding.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||DavidHenshaw||04-01-2001||12:01 AM||||Sorry, in my previous post I meant to say carbon on plugs indicate you are running too rich and thereby not getting the milage you should.<P>Dave||||reg||1
